On 16 Apr 2006, L wrote:
> practicality for trimming the '@' class. However, I feel that Keystone
> Kops are so inherently different to the military/mercenary humans (both
> the watch and the guards have M2_MERC flags, after all) that I feel
> grouping them together would be erronous.

I'll counter that the Minetown watch and the Vault guards are quite
different from the other "mercenaries" gameplay wise.  The watch/guards
only attack you if you provoke them, while the soldiers are always
hostile.

(While pedantically, the Kops are defined as "always hostile", they only
appear when you have made a provocation against a shopkeeper.)

In particular, this provides more -useful- information to the tileless
player (aside from the ';' or '/' commands).  In Minetown, it eliminates
the error of going out of one's way to avoid catching a "watchman" in
ranged fire, only to discover it was really a Soldier or Grey-Elf.

